sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Eligible participant
    participant UI as Review UI (proposed)
    participant API as Review API (proposed)
    participant S as Review service (proposed)
    participant DB as Review/history DB (proposed schema)
    Note over UI,DB: US14 conditional design - scope, eligibility, rating range, uniqueness and privacy await confirmation
    U->>UI: Select another participant, enter rating and review
    UI->>UI: Validate form, disable submit
    UI->>API: Proposed POST /api/v1/parties/{id}/reviews + session/CSRF
    alt Session / CSRF / input invalid
        API-->>UI: Validation/access error, re-enable form
    else Valid input
        API->>S: Validated target/rating/text, reviewer from session
        S->>DB: Read Party and shared participation history
        DB-->>S: End time, state and participation evidence
        S->>S: Confirm completed activity, eligibility and target != reviewer
        alt Not eligible / not completed / self-review
            S-->>API: Refuse per agreed contract
            API-->>UI: Error, no review stored
        else Eligible under confirmed policy
            S->>DB: BEGIN, insert Review using agreed unique constraint
            alt Duplicate or write failure
                S->>DB: ROLLBACK
                Note over S,DB: Catch unique conflict outside failed transaction, pre-check alone is insufficient
                S-->>API: Duplicate/error per contract
                API-->>UI: Explain failure, no duplicate success
            else Insert succeeds
                S->>DB: COMMIT
                S-->>API: Review saved
                API-->>UI: Success with public review fields
                UI->>API: Refresh reviews/rating summary (read contract TBD)
                API->>DB: Read allowed reviews and compute average stars
                DB-->>API: Reviews and star summary
                API-->>UI: Public allowlist, stars separate from conduct credit
                UI-->>U: Saved review and current summary
            end
        end
    end
    Note over UI,DB: No No-show report, threshold or conduct-credit mutation is implied by this diagram
